 The Shapley value is defined as follows:
\begin{multline}
\Phi(x_i) \\ =\sum_{S \subseteq \{1,\cdots,K\} \setminus \{i\}} \frac{|S|!(K-|S|-1)!}{K!}[f_{x}(S\cup\{i\})-f_{x}(S)]
\label{SHAPdef}
\end{multline}
, where $K$ is the number of stakeholders or features.

\Phi(x_i,x_j)$$
An interaction effect terms $\Phi(x_i,x_j)$ is defined as follows:
\begin{multline}
\Phi(x_i,x_j) \\ = \sum_{S\subseteq\{1,\cdots,K\}/\{i,j\}} \frac{2\cdot|S|!(K-|S|-1)!}{K!} [f_x(S\cup\{i,j\}) \\ - f_x(S\cup\{i\})-f_x(S\cup\{j\})+f_x(S)]
\end{multline}
A main effect terms $\Phi(x_i,x_i)$ is defined using the interaction terms $\Phi(x_i,x_j)$ and the Shapley values $\Phi(x_i)$.

